stream
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 800 Td (19. Why use async functions?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 787 Td (Answer: They help handle database and network operations efficiently.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 770 Td (20. What is middleware?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 757 Td (Answer: Code that runs before or after requests, such as CORS middleware.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 50 732 Td (Authentication) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 712 Td (21. How does registration work?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 699 Td (Answer: The backend validates user data, hashes the password, and stores the user.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 682 Td (22. How does login work?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 669 Td (Answer: The backend checks email/username and password, then returns tokens if valid.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 652 Td (23. Why do we hash passwords?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 639 Td (Answer: So original passwords are not stored and cannot be easily stolen.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 622 Td (24. Which hashing library is used?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 609 Td (Answer: Passlib with bcrypt.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 592 Td (25. What is bcrypt?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 579 Td (Answer: A secure password hashing algorithm designed to be slow against brute-force attacks.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 562 Td (26. How do you verify passwords?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 549 Td (Answer: Compare the plain password with the stored hash using verify_password\(\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 532 Td (27. What happens if credentials are invalid?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 519 Td (Answer: The backend returns an authentication error instead of a token.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 502 Td (28. What is the role of AuthService?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 489 Td (Answer: It contains authentication business logic.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 472 Td (29. What is the role of UserRepository?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 459 Td (Answer: It handles user-related database operations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 442 Td (30. Why not store password in plain text?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 429 Td (Answer: It is a serious security risk if the database is leaked.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 50 404 Td (JWT And Tokens) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 384 Td (31. What is JWT?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 371 Td (Answer: A signed token used to securely transfer user identity and claims.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 354 Td (32. Why did you use JWT?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 341 Td (Answer: It allows stateless authentication between frontend and backend.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 324 Td (33. What data is inside your token?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 311 Td (Answer: uid, email, username, role, expiry, jti, and refresh flag.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 294 Td (34. What is an access token?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 281 Td (Answer: A short-lived token used to access protected APIs.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 264 Td (35. What is a refresh token?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 251 Td (Answer: A longer-lived token used to generate a new access token.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 234 Td (36. Difference between access and refresh token?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 221 Td (Answer: Access token is for API access; refresh token is for renewing access.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 204 Td (37. Why does the access token expire?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 191 Td (Answer: To reduce damage if the token is stolen.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 174 Td (38. What is jti?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 161 Td (Answer: A unique token ID used for tracking and blacklisting tokens.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 144 Td (39. Why is uid validated as UUID?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 131 Td (Answer: To ensure token identity format is valid and safe.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 114 Td (40. What happens when a token expires?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 101 Td (Answer: The backend returns 401 Unauthorized.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 28 Td (Smart College Hub Backend Viva Questions | Page 2) Tj ET
endstream
