BT /F2 10 Tf 58 800 Td (41. What happens when a token is invalid?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 787 Td (Answer: The backend rejects it with an invalid token error.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 770 Td (42. How does logout work?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 757 Td (Answer: The token can be added to a blacklist so it cannot be reused.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 740 Td (43. Why use Redis for token blacklist?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 727 Td (Answer: Redis is fast and good for temporary token storage.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 710 Td (44. What is the JWT secret?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 697 Td (Answer: A private key used to sign and verify tokens.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 680 Td (45. Why store JWT secret in .env?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 667 Td (Answer: Secrets should not be hardcoded in source code.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 50 642 Td (Authorization And Roles) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 622 Td (46. What is authentication?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 609 Td (Answer: Checking who the user is.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 592 Td (47. What is authorization?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 579 Td (Answer: Checking what the user is allowed to do.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 562 Td (48. Difference between authentication and authorization?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 549 Td (Answer: Authentication verifies identity; authorization verifies permission.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 532 Td (49. What is role-based access control?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 519 Td (Answer: Access is allowed based on user roles such as student or admin.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 502 Td (50. How does RoleChecker work?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 489 Td (Answer: It checks if the current user's role is inside allowed_roles.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 472 Td (51. What happens if a user has no permission?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 459 Td (Answer: The backend returns 403 Forbidden.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 442 Td (52. Why protect routes?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 429 Td (Answer: To prevent unauthorized users from accessing private data or actions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 412 Td (53. Where is the current user retrieved?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 399 Td (Answer: From token data using get_current_user\(\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 50 374 Td (Database) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 354 Td (54. Which database layer is used?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 341 Td (Answer: SQLModel with SQLAlchemy async session.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 324 Td (55. What is SQLModel?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 311 Td (Answer: A library combining Pydantic-style validation with SQLAlchemy ORM features.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 294 Td (56. What is an ORM?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 281 Td (Answer: Object Relational Mapper; it maps Python classes to database tables.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 264 Td (57. Why use ORM?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 251 Td (Answer: It makes database operations easier and safer than raw SQL for common tasks.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 234 Td (58. What is AsyncSession?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 221 Td (Answer: An async database session used for non-blocking database operations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 204 Td (59. What does get_session\(\) do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 191 Td (Answer: It creates and yields a database session for each request.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 174 Td (60. What is DATABASE_URL?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 161 Td (Answer: The connection string used to connect the backend to the database.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 144 Td (61. What is a model?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 131 Td (Answer: A Python class that represents a database table.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 114 Td (62. What is a schema?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 101 Td (Answer: A validation and serialization structure for request and response data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 28 Td (Smart College Hub Backend Viva Questions | Page 3) Tj ET
endstream
