BT /F2 10 Tf 58 800 Td (63. Difference between model and schema?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 787 Td (Answer: Model maps to database; schema controls API data shape.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 770 Td (64. What is a primary key?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 757 Td (Answer: A unique identifier for each row in a table.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 740 Td (65. What is a foreign key?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 727 Td (Answer: A field that links one table to another table.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 710 Td (66. What is cascade delete?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 697 Td (Answer: Related child records are deleted when the parent record is deleted.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 680 Td (67. Why use indexes?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 667 Td (Answer: Indexes speed up searches and filtering on important columns.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 50 642 Td (Alembic Migrations) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 622 Td (68. What is Alembic?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 609 Td (Answer: A database migration tool for SQLAlchemy projects.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 592 Td (69. Why are migrations needed?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 579 Td (Answer: They track and apply database structure changes safely.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 562 Td (70. What is a migration file?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 549 Td (Answer: A versioned script that changes the database schema.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 532 Td (71. Why not manually edit database tables?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 519 Td (Answer: Manual changes are hard to track and can break team consistency.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 502 Td (72. How do migrations help deployment?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 489 Td (Answer: They let production database schema match the application code.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 472 Td (73. What happens when a model changes?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 459 Td (Answer: A new migration should be created and applied.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 442 Td (74. Why keep migration files in Git?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 429 Td (Answer: They document database history with the codebase.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 50 404 Td (CORS) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 384 Td (75. What is CORS?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 371 Td (Answer: A browser security rule controlling cross-origin frontend-backend requests.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 354 Td (76. Why did you add CORS middleware?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 341 Td (Answer: To allow the frontend running on localhost ports to call the backend.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 324 Td (77. What happens without CORS?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 311 Td (Answer: The browser may block frontend API requests.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 294 Td (78. Why list specific localhost origins?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 281 Td (Answer: It allows development frontend URLs without opening the API to every origin.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 264 Td (79. What does allow_methods=['*'] mean?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 251 Td (Answer: All HTTP methods like GET, POST, PUT, DELETE are allowed.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 234 Td (80. What does allow_headers=['*'] mean?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 221 Td (Answer: All request headers are allowed.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 204 Td (81. What does allow_credentials=True mean?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 191 Td (Answer: Credentials such as auth headers can be included in requests.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 174 Td (82. Should all origins be allowed in production?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 161 Td (Answer: No, production should allow only trusted domains.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 50 136 Td (Collaboration Module) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 116 Td (83. What is the collaboration feature?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 103 Td (Answer: It lets users create, join, and manage collaboration groups/projects.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 28 Td (Smart College Hub Backend Viva Questions | Page 4) Tj ET
endstream
