BT /F2 10 Tf 58 800 Td (84. Why separate collaboration routes?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 787 Td (Answer: To keep collaboration logic organized and independent.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 770 Td (85. What is a join request?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 757 Td (Answer: A request from a user to join a collaboration.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 740 Td (86. What is membership?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 727 Td (Answer: A record showing that a user belongs to a collaboration.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 710 Td (87. Difference between owner and member?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 697 Td (Answer: Owner manages the collaboration; member participates in it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 680 Td (88. How do you prevent duplicate membership?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 667 Td (Answer: Using service checks or database constraints.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 650 Td (89. How are join requests approved?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 637 Td (Answer: The owner/admin accepts the request and membership is created.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 620 Td (90. What happens when a collaboration is deleted?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 607 Td (Answer: Related memberships and requests can be removed through cascade rules.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 590 Td (91. Why have separate join request and membership tables?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 577 Td (Answer: A request is pending approval; membership means the user has joined.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 560 Td (92. What validation is needed in collaboration APIs?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 547 Td (Answer: Check ownership, membership status, duplicate requests, and permissions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 50 522 Td (Coding Challenge Module) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 502 Td (93. What is the coding challenge module?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 489 Td (Answer: It manages coding problems and student submissions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 472 Td (94. Who can create challenges?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 459 Td (Answer: Challenge creation should be limited to authorized users such as admins or teachers) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 447 Td (so students cannot modify official challenge content.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 430 Td (95. What is a submission?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 417 Td (Answer: A student's answer or code submitted for a challenge.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 400 Td (96. Why store submission feedback?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 387 Td (Answer: So students can see evaluation comments or results.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 370 Td (97. Why add submission indexes?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 357 Td (Answer: To make submission searches and filters faster.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 340 Td (98. How does the backend validate challenge data?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 327 Td (Answer: Using schemas and service-layer checks.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 310 Td (99. What endpoints are expected for challenges?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 297 Td (Answer: Create, list, detail, update, delete, and submit.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 280 Td (100. What improvement could be added?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 267 Td (Answer: Automatic code execution, test cases, leaderboard, and plagiarism checks.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 50 242 Td (Repository And Service Pattern) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 222 Td (101. What is repository pattern?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 209 Td (Answer: A layer that handles database queries separately from business logic.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 192 Td (102. What is a service layer?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 179 Td (Answer: A layer that contains business rules and coordinates repositories.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 162 Td (103. Why not write everything in route files?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 149 Td (Answer: Routes become messy and hard to test if they contain all logic.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 132 Td (104. What belongs in routes?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 119 Td (Answer: Request/response handling, dependencies, and calling services.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 58 102 Td (105. What belongs in services?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 89 Td (Answer: Business logic such as validation, permissions, and workflows.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50 28 Td (Smart College Hub Backend Viva Questions | Page 5) Tj ET
endstream
